        "text": "For each increase of 1 in y, x decreases by about 2.",
        "rationale": "This reverses the roles of x and y."
      },
      {
        "id": "C",
        "text": "For each increase of 1 in x, y increases by about 2.",
        "rationale": "The sign of the slope gives the direction of change."
      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "For each increase of 1 in x, y decreases by about 8.",
        "rationale": "That is the y-intercept's value, not the slope."
      },
      {
        "id": "E",
        "text": "For each increase of 1 in x, y decreases by about 2.",
        "rationale": "Correct."
      }
    ],
    "correct_choice": "E",
    "explanation": "In y = −2x − 8, the slope −2 is the predicted change in y per unit increase in x.",
